1.2.15</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">D</span> POSITION. In poets <span class=\"gk\">ἀμφί</span> sts. follows its case, <span class=\"gk\">οἱ δέ μιν ἀμφί</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">23.46</span> </span>, cf. <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">10.218</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">B.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">17.53</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">φρένας ἀ.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Hes.</span> <cite class=\"lex-cite-title\">Th.</cite> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">554</span> </span>, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Mimn.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.7</span> </span>; but never suffers anastrophe, Hdn.Gr.<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">1.480</span> </span>. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"1\"><span class=\"lex-n\">E</span> WITHOUT CASE, as <span class=\"lex-gram\">Adv.</span>, <b class=\"lex-tr\">about, around, on both</b> or <b class=\"lex-tr\">all sides,</b> freq. in <span class=\"lex-gram\"> <span class=\"lex-gram\">Ep.</span> </span>, <span class=\"gk\">ῥῆξεν δέ οἱ ἀ. χιτῶνα</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">13.439</span> </span>; <span class=\"gk\">ἀ. δὲ λειμών</span> <b class=\"lex-tr\">around</b> is meadow, <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Od.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">6.292</span> </span>; so <span class=\"gk\">ἀ. περί</span> <span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">Il.</span> <span class=\"lex-cite-scope\">21.10</span> </span>, etc. </div> <div class=\"lex-sense\" data-level=\"2\"><span class=\"lex-n\">F</span> IN COMPO<span class=\"lex-cite\"> <span class=\"lex-cite-author\">S.</span> </span>: </div> <div clas